.TH REMAIL 1 "2026-09-12" "remail 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
remail \- a fast IMAP and Gmail client
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B remail
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B remail
is a desktop email client. It talks to Gmail over OAuth2 and to any IMAP
server with a password or app password, caches mailboxes, envelopes and
message bodies in SQLite so that opening a folder paints from cache in the
same frame, and parks a second connection in
.B IDLE
per account so new mail arrives without polling.
.PP
It takes no command-line arguments. Accounts are added from
.B Accounts
in the application itself.
.PP
Message bodies are sanitized before they are drawn: scripts, frames, event
handlers and
.B javascript:
URLs are removed outright, and remote images are withheld until you ask for
them, because a uniquely named remote image is the standard read receipt.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B REMAIL_LOG
Tracing filter directives, in the syntax used by
.BR tracing-subscriber (3).
When unset, the default is
.BR "remail=info,warn,fontdb=error" .
Set
.B REMAIL_LOG=remail=debug
to see the IMAP command traffic.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/remail/config.toml
Accounts, theme, per-pane fonts and pane widths. Written when a setting
changes.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/remail/cache.sqlite
Mailbox, envelope and body cache, along with remembered remote-content
permissions and the addresses used for recipient completion. Safe to delete;
it is rebuilt from the server.
.PP
Passwords and OAuth refresh tokens are not written to either. They are held
in the platform keyring via
.BR libsecret (3);
if no keyring is available, the application says so and asks for the password
each session.
.SH SEE ALSO
Project homepage:
.UR https://github.com/ahenshaw/remail
.UE
